# Intent: The face detection experiment can be built (owner brief 2026-11-17, docs/design/face-detect-esp-dl-2026-11-17.md). The existing Kconfig switch MAIPAI_FACE_DETECT (default n) now builds instead of stopping the build: the #error that reserved it is gone. With the switch on, main/idf_component.yml pulls espressif/esp-dl exactly 3.3.15 and espressif/human_face_detect exactly 0.5.2 through the component manager (a `$CONFIG{MAIPAI_FACE_DETECT} == True` rule, so with the switch off neither component is in the build), esp-dl needs esp_new_jpeg ^1 where the image has always used 0.6.1, so that one dependency carries two `matches` rules (^1.0.0 with the switch on, ^0.6.1 with it off: the plain image keeps its old version), main/CMakeLists.txt links both components into main only when the switch is on (idf_component_optional_requires), and the new overlay sdkconfig.fdetect.defaults (bench image only, rides on sdkconfig.bench.defaults and sdkconfig.gate.defaults) turns on both model families (MSR plus MNP, 191 KB, and ESPDet-Pico 224, 480 KB) as read-only data in the app image (MODEL_LOCATION_IN_FLASH_RODATA: no partition change, no assets or pack cache change). New Kconfig (all under the switch): the default model (MSR plus MNP or Pico 224), the rate (2 to 5 a second, default 3), the score floor (50 percent), the unload delay (10 s), the admission floor (40,000 internal bytes free and a 24,000 byte block), and the tracker switches of patch FD04 (MAIPAI_FACE_TRACK default n, MAIPAI_FACE_TRACK_TILT default n, MAIPAI_FACE_TRACK_HOUR_MIN default 10). The experiment image does not fit the 5 MB app slot with the library, so: maipai_facedet.compile_req.yml (made by scripts/fw-facedet-req.py) tells esp-dl to compile only the 15 operators and 36 eight-bit kernels the face models use (the library drops from 1.44 MB to about 0.7 MB), and with the switch on the build leaves out the generated maipai_bench_clips.c (562 KB of voice bench clips, made by scripts/fw-bench-clips.py) and links the new maipai_bench_clips_stub.c, seven one-sample silences, instead (the voice bench is not meant to run on that image). Nothing else is added: no source file, no task, no tool.
# Placement: unit (build plumbing; the experiment image only, off in every shipped image)
# Upstream: firmware/main/idf_component.yml, main/CMakeLists.txt, main/Kconfig.projbuild, main/hal/maipai_seek.cc (the reserved #error, patch S14); new firmware/sdkconfig.fdetect.defaults. Packages: espressif/esp-dl 3.3.15 (MIT), espressif/human_face_detect 0.5.2 (MIT, weights under the folder's MIT LICENSE; training data terms not stated), espressif/esp_new_jpeg 1.0.x for the experiment image only
# Check after a flash: nothing to check on a unit (no code yet). Build check: `build.sh build-plain sdkconfig.fplain ""` still gives the plain image its old size and its esp_new_jpeg 0.6.1 (dependencies.lock), and `build.sh build-fdetect sdkconfig.fdetect "sdkconfig.bench.defaults;sdkconfig.gate.defaults;sdkconfig.fdetect.defaults"` configures with both components and both models in the app image.

